                                                "sense_id": "0d23f40a-7908-3724-b6c6-07803809d92f",
                                                "text": "Holmes, who loathed every form of society with his whole Bohemian soul, remained in our lodgings in Baker-street, buried among his old books, and alternating from week to week between cocaine and ambition, the drowsiness of the drug, and the fierce energy of his own keen nature."
